# This repo is PUBLIC. Deploy credentials live outside the tree
# (~/.config/kilokaki-site/deploy.env). These patterns are belt-and-braces
# in case someone drops a filled-in copy here by mistake.
deploy.env
*.env
!*.env.example
.DS_Store

# --- Debris suppression for the self-verify gate (scripts/deploy.sh) ---
# SELF_VERIFY runs `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` and aborts on
# ANY untracked file, because RSYNC_FILTER ships by glob and rsync walks the
# filesystem, not the index. That strictness is the point. But it means routine
# local debris would block a legitimate deploy, and a gate that cries wolf gets
# --force'd past — trading a silent ship for a worn-out alarm. So ignore the
# debris, and ONLY the debris.
#
# CORRECTION, 2026-07-22 (Coco). This block used to end: "nothing here can match
# a shippable page, asset, or script, so the gate still fires on every file that
# could reach the CDN." That was FALSE, and it is the sentence a reviewer would
# have trusted instead of re-deriving. `._*` is a PREFIX pattern, so `._draft.html`
# is ignored here AND matches --include='/blog/*.html' in RSYNC_FILTER — rsync
# globs are not shell globs and a leading dot is not special. Measured: four
# paths shipped (blog/._ghost.html, blog/._sidecar.png, how-to/._ghost.html,
# ._style.css). Every other pattern below is suffix- or literal-matched and
# genuinely cannot reach the CDN; `._*` was the only one.
#
# The real guard is now --exclude='._*' as the FIRST rule of RSYNC_FILTER, where
# rsync's first-match-wins makes it unshippable. This entry is back to being a
# convenience. scripts/test-rsync-filter.sh holds it to that.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
._*
.AppleDouble
Thumbs.db
